## What this is

OpenRewrite recipes, published to Maven Central as `{{ repo.package }}`.

The catalog is the only coordinate you write down. It carries two recipes as YAML and pulls in
`recipes-minecraft-invui`, the Java module holding the visitors one of them calls.

`de.timscho.rewrite.Style` applies the static analysis a formatter cannot, because every rule in it
changes what the code does rather than how it is laid out.
`de.timscho.rewrite.minecraft.invui.v1-to-v2` migrates a Bukkit plugin from InvUI 1.x to 2.x,
rewriting what it can and marking what it cannot.

## Quick start

```kotlin
// build.gradle.kts
plugins {
    id("org.openrewrite.rewrite") version "7.39.0"
}

rewrite {
    activeRecipe("de.timscho.rewrite.Style")
}

dependencies {
    rewrite("{{ repo.package }}:{{ release.version }}")
}
```

```bash
./gradlew rewriteDryRun
```

The patch lands in `build/reports/rewrite/rewrite.patch`. Your sources are untouched until you run
`rewriteRun`.

